  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v9.1.0: Adds IAsyncDisposable — `await using` is now the preferred lifecycle; DisposeAsync awaits the RFC 6455 close handshake before releasing the socket, Dispose stays bounded best-effort. Connection teardown is unified: the close runs exactly once on every end path (completion, error, unsubscribe, dispose) via one shared mechanism. Read-loop errors now reliably reach the subscriber as OnError instead of racing teardown into a silent completion. Removes the public ObservableExtensions.FinallyAsync operator (unsound: never fired on unsubscribe). Upgrades HttpMachine.PCL to 6.0.1 (span-based, allocation-free handshake parsing; case-insensitive headers). See README for details.",
